workbook :native_cli_integration, type: :design

# Native CLI integration — how we wire each of the 98 official CLIs into the wasm sandbox

The OpenAPI engine (registry/integration-cli-strategy.work, prototype: src/lib/dock/cli-engine.js) covers the
SPEC-based providers. The 98 with an OFFICIAL CLI are different: we capture the integration by compiling the
REAL CLI binary to WebAssembly and running it in our sandbox. The guest CLI believes it is real; the HOST
(Dock/WASI) provides: the **network** (host fetch to the provider's API hosts), **secrets** (injected via
Nexus.Secrets into the guest env — never authored, never in the guest image), a **virtual FS** (for the
config/token files a CLI expects), and stdio. Profiled by a 10-agent workflow (native-cli-deep-dive).

## Two axes decide every integration

**1. wasm portability (by impl language).** Go/Rust/Zig/C compile to wasm32-wasi cleanly; Node/Python CLIs
need their RUNTIME shipped too (our compilers lane has QuickJS / a python-on-wasm path, hence 'hard' not
impossible). Languages seen: node 34 · go 33 · python 17 · php 5 · rust 4 · c 2 · java 2 · objc 1.

- ready (go/rust/c, direct): **34**  ·  feasible: **4**  ·  hard (node/python, needs runtime): **55**  ·  blocked: **5**

**2. auth method.** The headless-friendly ones (env key / config token) just need a secret injected. The
browser-login ones CANNOT run headless — we must use their env/token fallback and seed a config file so the
guest skips the browser flow.

- mixed: **41**
- config-file-token: **19** (headless-ok)
- oauth-browser-login: **12** (needs token fallback)
- env-api-key: **10** (headless-ok)
- none: **7** (headless-ok)
- interactive-login: **6** (needs token fallback)
- oauth-device-flow: **2** (headless-ok)
- cloud-iam: **1** (headless-ok)

## Port order

**Tier A — port first: wasm-ready + headless auth.** Compile the Go/Rust binary, inject one secret, proxy the
host fetch. No browser, no runtime, no config seeding. The cleanest wins:

integration_cli :tier_a_port_first do
  cli "Apollo", bin: "rover", lang: :rust, auth: :config_file_token, secret: "APOLLO_KEY"
  cli "Auth0", bin: "auth0", lang: :go, auth: :oauth_device_flow, secret: "AUTH0_CLIENT_ID"
  cli "DigitalOcean", bin: "doctl", lang: :go, auth: :config_file_token, secret: "DIGITALOCEAN_ACCESS_TOKEN"
  cli "Grafana", bin: "grafana-cli", lang: :go, auth: :none, secret: "GF_PLUGIN_DIR"
  cli "Incident.io", bin: "catalog-importer", lang: :go, auth: :env_api_key, secret: "INCIDENT_API_KEY"
  cli "Lokalise", bin: "lokalise2", lang: :go, auth: :env_api_key, secret: "LOKALISE_API_TOKEN"
  cli "Resend", bin: "resend", lang: :go, auth: :env_api_key, secret: "RESEND_API_KEY"
  cli "Sentry", bin: "sentry-cli", lang: :rust, auth: :env_api_key, secret: "SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN"
  cli "Supabase", bin: "supabase", lang: :go, auth: :config_file_token, secret: "SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN"
  cli "Terraform", bin: "terraform", lang: :go, auth: :cloud_iam, secret: "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"
  cli "Twitch", bin: "twitch", lang: :go, auth: :config_file_token, secret: "TWITCH_CLIENT_ID"
  cli "Wakatime", bin: "wakatime-cli", lang: :go, auth: :config_file_token, secret: "WAKATIME_API_KEY"
  cli "WorkOS", bin: "workos", lang: :go, auth: :env_api_key, secret: "WORKOS_API_KEY"
end

